From tru64-unix-managers  Fri Jan 26 15:07:43 2001
From: "Todd B. Acheson" <acheson () ohiou ! edu>
Date: Fri, 26 Jan 2001 15:07:43 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: 5.1 +pk2 processes stuck in 'U' state
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=98052278703229


Answer:

We verified with Compaq that the Cyrus IMAP daemon processes that we 
daily found stuck in a 'U' state (necessitating reboots)  were 
exercising the same lock/race condition that I discovered 2.5 years ago
in 4.0B and got fixed at that time. It was disappointing to have had to
revisit this painful problem.

Engineering provided a fix that I have run for 36 hours with great 
success. This fix may make it into patch kit 3 for 5.1, but I am not
sure.

If you believe you are experiencing this problem and need more 
informatioin to get the fix from compaq, please contact me.

The original problem statement was:

> I just went production with 5.1+patch kit 2 on an ES40.  this is a
> very, very busy system serving primarily as an IMAP server.  This
> system was upgraded from a 4100 running 4.0F.
>
> I am seeing Cyrus IMAP processes sticking permanently in a 'U' state.
>
> I had this same situation occur over 2 years ago on 4.0B/4.0D.  It was
> caused by a race condition in the ADVFS/kernel and required some
> extensive rewrites of ADVFS code which were incorporated into 4.0D in a
> patch kit.
>
> I am wondering if the fixes that went into the 4.0x stream did not make
> it into the 5.x code stream.
>
----------------------
Todd Acheson
740 593-0034

acheson@ohiou.edu

