--- anthony.miller@vf.vodafone.co.uk wrote:
> Try this.
>=20
> Tony
>=20
>=20
> =B7 Set up the Login Banner
>=20
> For security, the system type and name should be
> removed from any login
> banner. At present the Dunix default is to provide
> the System type, version,
> hostname and terminal name prior to the login
> prompt. To remove this follow
> these steps:-
>=20
> Ensure a file /etc/issue exists and is of the form
> shown below.  Note that #
> denotes start and end of file - so don't actually
> add these to the file:
>=20
> #
>=20
> Unauthorised access to the system is an offense
> pursuant to the Computer misuse act 1990
> #
>=20
> The file should be owned by root:system and have 444
> permission.
>=20
> Copy the file /etc/gettydefs to /etc/gettydefs.orig.
>=20
> Edit /etc/gettydefs and make the following
> amendments.  Add the following
> line to the beginning of the file (after the
> comments).  Note: this must be
> preceded by a blank line.
> =09default###\r\n#default
>=20
> Replace line
> =09console# B9600 HUPCL CS8 CLOCAL IXON OPOST ONLCR #
> B9600 SANE
> IXANY TAB3 CLOCAL #\r\n\r\n%v (%h)
> %t\r\n\r\n\rlogin: #console
> with
> =09console# B9600 HUPCL CS8 CLOCAL IXON OPOST ONLCR #
> B9600 SANE
> IXANY TAB3 CLOCAL #login: #console
>=20
> So any login to the system will now be of the form:-
>=20
> Unauthorised access to the system is an offence
> persuant to the Computer misuse act 1990
>=20
> login:
>=20
> instead of:-
>=20
> Unauthorised access to the system is an offence
