> Hi, just a quick question.
>=20
> We are currently running Tru64 4.0F, and are ready to upgrade to =
version
> 5.0a.  My question is, if it turns out something doesn't work in the =
new
> version, is it possible to revert back to 4.0F?  If so, is it a
> complicated task?  I browsed through the software documentation, and
> didn't redily see this topic covered.  Does anyone know where I could
> find detailed instructions?  Thanks in advance..
>=20
> Jonathan Williams

Just wanted to say "thank you" to the masses of people that responded to =
my question.  The answer is pretty much unanimous:

BACKUP BACKUP BACKUP BACKUP BACKUP!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!
(and have backups of your backups!!)

There is simply no easy way to get back out of the upgrade, so you would =
have to restore everything from your backups.  A few people suggested =
actually using a spare disk and make a copy of your system disk, so you =
could just pop in the copy and boot from it.  Or if you don't have a =
spare disk (like me) and your system supports it (unlike me) you could =
make a bootable tape backup!!  Pretty cool stuff.  Thanks again to all =
who replied. =20

-Jonathan Williams

