Subject: ADVFSD High CPU Problem
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=97994038615185

The ADVFSD process on our Alphaserver 1000a/400, Unix 4.0D, once in a while
(every 30 - 60 days), will get "crazy" and start grabbing 60 to 80% of the
CPU.  The ADVFS GUI still works, but this slows downs our system enough to
cause time-out problems on our time sensitive applications.  To get around
the problem we kill and restart the process.

QUESTION:
Has anyone seen this before, and if so what is causing the process to do
this?

John Pshyk
E-mail: john.pshyk@atcoelectric.com

