> Hello,
> 
> Does anyone have a good grasp as to what "CPU Machine Check Errors" are?  They
> are being reported by dia as "620 System Correctable Error" and I have searched
> the archive for a SUMMARY related to this message (which I assume is common
> since there are many postings by people asking what the error might mean) but
> I see none.
> 
> Many thanks,
> Bill Antoniadis

Many thanks to all who responded.  Everybody agreed that "machine check errors"
are hardware detected errors (in my case, memory errors).  Usually these errors 
occur during a memory, or a cache read (for example, a parity read error may 
occur).  Though these are correctable errors (with ECC memory), too many errors 
can hurt overall system performance.

Regards,
Bill Antoniadis

