From: Dan Kirkpatrick <dkirk () suhep ! phy ! syr ! edu>
Date: Sun, 14 Jan 2001 14:40:08 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: error "NFS Portmap: RPC: Program not registered"
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=97948307918230

Thanks for the quick help on a weekend from "Sean O'Connell" 
<sean@stat.Duke.EDU> and BrianH@dice.com

in the end, the machine serving the disk was blocking through security....
The final fix was to add:
portmap: 128.230.72.0/255.255.255.0
rpc.nfsd: 128.230.72.0/255.255.255.0
rpc.mountd: 128.230.72.0/255.255.255.0
to /etc/hosts.allow
(The machine serving the disk incidently is Linux, the servers trying to 
mount it are Dec unix 4.0B)

Also part of the troubleshooting process was to make sure rpc.statd and 
lockd are running, as well as portmap.  (rpcinfo -p localhost), make sure 
the disk is shared correctly in /etc/exports, and make sure nfs is running.

Thanks!  My department is back online now!
--Dan

