The answer from Colin Walters was what I want:

We do not recommend manual edits to modify user accounts.

Use the CDE dxaccounts utility to select the user account and
then edit the username.  All required system files are updated
automatically.

Or see:  SysMan Accounts
         usermod command
---------------------------------------------------------------------------=
----------------------------------
But if you want to do manualy don't forget
- renaming user in /etc/passwd
- renaming cron file
- renaming mail file
- renaming the user in /etc/group
- renaming user home directory if apply
- and all scripts that have reference with that user or user home =
directory.
---------------------------------------------------------------------------=
