From: George Mpitsos <george.mpitsos () hmsc ! orst ! edu>
Date: Thu, 11 Jan 2001 21:15:56 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY-2 Unsupported Systems
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=97924763427930

Good and bad news on support for 2100 Alphas.  My thanks again to 
Rodney Dollar at ComPaq pre-sales tech support.

>From 
http://www5.compaq.com/products/quickspecs/10513_na/10513_na.HTML we 
get the info that Tru64Unix V5.1 supports the 2100 machines.

But, as I mentioned in the first SUMMARY report, the 2100 machines 
are "retired"  and testing and maintenance of support on particular 
devices is up to individual managers. I.e., with luck the particular 
devices in a machine might work OK.

Feedback from pre-sales software tech support indicated that the 
KZPSC RAID controller on my machine will work with V5.1, and this 
appears to be varified from info listed in 
http://www5.compaq.com/alphaserver/options/2x00_restrictions.html.

However, I persisted a bit further and got the following reply from 
pre-sales software tech support:


"George, this is the final word--- not supported. It will probably work

Copyright 1999 Compaq Computer Corporation.  All rights reserved

SOURCE:  Compaq Computer Corporation         INFORMATION   BLITZ

INFORMATION BLITZ TITLE:

     KZESC and KZPSC RAID controllers will not be supported on Tru64 UNIX 5.x

DATE: Apr 9, 1999"


Please note, the "It will probably" work. I take this to mean that 
the KZPSC has probably not been tested with FW/OS versions CD5.8/5.1, 
and because the device is "not supported", firmware support will not 
be upgraded for it if needed. I.e., caveat emptor!

Also note that the firmware release notes for the 2100 machines 
http://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/readmes/v5.8/doc/ are 
dated Dec, 1999, but, if I recall correctly from the FW 5.4 CD, are 
the same as in earlier FW releases.

For 2100 owners who wish to upgrade to OS V5.x, or those above V4.0f. 
I would not take it for granted from listing in documents as those 
referred to above that the devices will in fact work. I suggest 
sending a description of the devices on your machine to a contact 
person at pre-sales software support (800.354.9000) where your 
questions will be referred to the appropriate engineers.

I've opted to go ahead and try FW/OS CD versions 5.8/5.1.

george






