MacDonell, Dennis [DennisMacDonell@auslig.gov.au]

Special thanks to James and Joerg, as their variations worked.

There were a variety of answers, including escaping the "!", looking through
the proc man page, a corruption of procfs (this worries me!), and this is
the behavior of find.

Further investigation is below. The command that worked:

find / -fstype procfs -prune -o -name "core" -ctime +10 -exec echo {} \;

Suggestions were made to specify the file systems we wanted searched. This
was not an option for us, this server has 3 ESA12000 connected to it, and
file systems come and go at a high rate. We will add 1.2TB to it in the next
year.

The behavior of either the shell or find has changed. Whether this is a bug
or not is an internal issue for Compaq. The find command varies from 4.x to
5.0. There is also some issues with the procfs see 0642 is in the ls, but
not the ls -al nor the lsof...

This may be a time to call Compaq <grin>....

Are people finding 5.1 stable? i.e. are the bug / patch rates now lower in
5.1 than 5.0?

Cheers,

Guy

